---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Install from '../components/Install.astro';

const REPO = 'https://github.com/Tulum-DAO/orchestraos';
---

<Base
  surface="home"
  title="OrchestraOS by Tulum DAO"
  description="OrchestraOS is an open harness for running a fleet of coding agents as a team. Clone it from github.com/Tulum-DAO/orchestraos and run make install."
>
  <div id="backdrop" aria-hidden="true"></div>
  <canvas id="cenote" aria-hidden="true"></canvas>
  <div id="cenote-labels" aria-hidden="true"></div>

  <section class="hero" data-bg="#e9e3d3" data-depth="0">
    <div class="hero-copy">
      <h1>Run a fleet of coding agents as a team.</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        OrchestraOS is an open harness, published by Tulum DAO. Agents message each other, remember
        across restarts, rotate themselves before they run out of context, and put every real decision
        in front of you on your phone.
      </p>
      <a class="repo" href={REPO}>
        <svg viewBox="0 0 16 16" width="22" height="22" aria-hidden="true"
          ><path
            fill="currentColor"
            d="M8 0C3.58 0 0 3.58 0 8c0 3.54 2.29 6.53 5.47 7.59.4.07.55-.17.55-.38 0-.19-.01-.82-.01-1.49-2.01.37-2.53-.49-2.69-.94-.09-.23-.48-.94-.82-1.13-.28-.15-.68-.52-.01-.53.63-.01 1.08.58 1.23.82.72 1.21 1.87.87 2.33.66.07-.52.28-.87.51-1.07-1.78-.2-3.64-.89-3.64-3.95 0-.87.31-1.59.82-2.15-.08-.2-.36-1.02.08-2.12 0 0 .67-.21 2.2.82.64-.18 1.32-.27 2-.27.68 0 1.36.09 2 .27 1.53-1.04 2.2-.82 2.2-.82.44 1.1.16 1.92.08 2.12.51.56.82 1.27.82 2.15 0 3.07-1.87 3.75-3.65 3.95.29.25.54.73.54 1.48 0 1.07-.01 1.93-.01 2.2 0 .21.15.46.55.38A8.013 8.013 0 0016 8c0-4.42-3.58-8-8-8z"
          ></path></svg
        >
        <span class="repo-path"><span class="repo-host">github.com/</span>Tulum-DAO/orchestraos</span>
      </a>
    </div>
    <div class="hero-install">
      <Install />
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="honest" data-bg="#bfdcd6" data-depth="0.12">
    <h2>Build with us</h2>
    <p>
      OrchestraOS is built in the open, and the community is always making contributions to the build. It
      runs one operator's fleet every day, and that setup is the reference install. Pick a track or a good
      first issue and add yours.
    </p>
  </section>

  <div class="descent">
    <section class="layer" data-bg="#2f8580" data-depth="0.3" data-layer="seats">
      <div class="panel">
        <h2>Seats and generations</h2>
        <p class="short">
          Each agent is a seat. Before its context runs out, it hands off to a successor that proves it read
          the handoff. <a href="/docs/rotation/">How rotation works</a>
        </p>
        <p class="long">
          An agent is a seat with a lineage. Each generation is one CLI session: Claude Code, Gemini or
          Codex. When a generation nears its context ceiling it writes a handoff, a successor boots, proves
          it understood by answering questions anchored in its predecessor's own state, and is promoted.
        </p>
        <p class="aside long">
          Rotation is on by default for Claude seats. Gemini and Codex are experimental and stay unarmed
          until you opt in. <a href="/docs/rotation/">How rotation works</a>
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="layer" data-bg="#0b4f52" data-depth="0.5" data-layer="messages">
      <div class="panel">
        <h2>Smart inter-agent messaging that doesn't interrupt work</h2>
        <p class="short">Agents hand each other work. Mail for a busy agent waits until its turn ends.</p>
        <p class="long">
          Agents hand each other work through a durable message store with inboxes, acknowledgements and
          threads. Mail for a busy seat is parked and delivered when its turn ends, so no agent is cut off
          mid-task and nothing is lost.
        </p>
        <ul class="legend" aria-label="Message types in the animation">
          <li><span style="--c:#ff8a6b"></span>task</li>
          <li><span style="--c:#a8e06a"></span>reply</li>
          <li><span style="--c:#b39dff"></span>task_complete</li>
          <li><span style="--c:#ff5fa8"></span>escalate</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="layer" data-bg="#093a3c" data-depth="0.7" data-layer="memory">
      <div class="panel">
        <h2>Memory that survives a restart</h2>
        <p class="short">Facts and each seat's memory outlive every restart and rotation.</p>
        <p class="long">
          A shared facts store with freshness, memory directories for each seat that outlive rotation, and a
          recall hook that feeds Arturo, the assistant.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="layer" data-bg="#0a2a2b" data-depth="0.88" data-layer="approvals">
      <div class="panel">
        <h2>Every real decision comes up to you</h2>
        <p class="short">
          Anything an agent needs from you is a card on your phone, watch or dashboard. Your answer resumes it.
        </p>
        <p class="long">
          Anything an agent needs from you is a card: approve or deny, a menu, a questionnaire, or a
          "waiting on you" block. Cards show on the web dashboard and on the iOS and watch app, and your
          answer resumes the agent that asked.
        </p>
        <p class="aside long">
          The runtime catalog checks which CLIs you have installed and logged in to, so the harness runs on a
          subscription you already pay for.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>

  <section class="paths" data-bg="#12201f" data-depth="1">
    <h2>Two ways to run it</h2>
    <div class="path-grid">
      <a class="path" href="/docs/install/">
        <h3>The minimum path</h3>
        <p class="short">One machine, one CLI. About an hour the first time, from nothing.</p>
        <p class="long">
          One machine, one CLI, no voice, no chat bridges. From nothing to a VPS on your Tailscale network,
          the dashboard open in your browser over https, one seat spawned and one card answered. Budget
          about an hour the first time.
        </p>
        <span class="go">Start here</span>
      </a>
      <a class="path" href="/docs/reference-install/">
        <h3>The reference install</h3>
        <p class="short">The operator's own setup: VPS plus Mac, push, Telegram and voice. Do this second.</p>
        <p class="long">
          The operator's own setup: a VPS plus a Mac over Tailscale, tmux seats, the rotation beat, push
          notifications, Telegram and voice. Do this second.
        </p>
        <span class="go">Read the reference install</span>
      </a>
    </div>
    <ul class="more">
      <li><a href="/docs/beginners-guide/">Never used a terminal? The beginner's guide</a></li>
      <li><a href="/docs/costs/">What a VPS and a CLI plan cost, and the no-cost option</a></li>
      <li><a href="/docs/onboarding/">Connect your phone and browser to your gateway</a></li>
      <li><a href="/docs/architecture/">The architecture map</a></li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="build" data-bg="#12201f" data-depth="1">
    <h2>How to contribute</h2>
    <p>
      Fork the repo, branch, and open a pull request against <code>main</code>. CI runs the tests for each
      package and a secrets scan, and both must pass. Sign off your commits (DCO). There are thirteen tracks,
      each with its own doc and a start prompt you can paste into your own agent, and a list of small
      good-first issues.
    </p>
    <p class="links">
      <a href={`${REPO}/blob/main/docs/tracks/README.md`}>The thirteen tracks</a>
      <a href={`${REPO}/blob/main/docs/HACKATHON_ISSUES.md`}>Good first issues</a>
      <a href={`${REPO}/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md`}>Contributing</a>
    </p>
  </section>
</Base>

<script>
  // Progressive enhancement: everything above renders without this. The scene loads after first
  // paint, only when the browser is idle, and never when the visitor asked for reduced motion.
  const reduce = matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)');
  const canvas = document.getElementById('cenote') as HTMLCanvasElement;
  // A software rasteriser (no GPU: SwiftShader, llvmpipe) would draw every frame on the main
  // thread and make the page janky, so it gets the static page and never downloads Three.js.
  const hardwareGL = () => {
    try {
      const gl = document.createElement('canvas').getContext('webgl2') ?? document.createElement('canvas').getContext('webgl');
      if (!gl) return false;
      const info = gl.getExtension('WEBGL_debug_renderer_info');
      const name = String(gl.getParameter(info ? info.UNMASKED_RENDERER_WEBGL : gl.RENDERER));
      gl.getExtension('WEBGL_lose_context')?.loseContext();
      return !/swiftshader|llvmpipe|softpipe|software|basic render/i.test(name);
    } catch {
      return false;
    }
  };
  const start = () => {
    // ?cenote forces the scene on a software renderer (for screenshots); reduced motion still wins
    const force = new URLSearchParams(location.search).has('cenote');
    if (reduce.matches || !(force || hardwareGL())) return;
    import('../scripts/cenote').then((m) => m.mount(canvas)).catch(() => {});
  };
  const idle = (fn: () => void) =>
    'requestIdleCallback' in window ? requestIdleCallback(fn, { timeout: 2500 }) : setTimeout(fn, 1200);
  if (document.readyState === 'complete') idle(start);
  else addEventListener('load', () => idle(start), { once: true });
</script>

<style>
  #backdrop,
  #cenote {
    position: fixed;
    inset: 0;
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
  }
  /* The backdrop keeps pointer events (it is under everything anyway) so contrast checkers,
     which find backgrounds with elementsFromPoint, see the water colour behind the text. */
  #cenote {
    pointer-events: none;
  }
  #backdrop {
    z-index: 0;
    background: var(--limestone);
    display: none;
  }
  #cenote {
    z-index: 1;
    opacity: 0;
    transition: opacity 1.2s ease;
  }
  /* seat names drawn over the scene (example names), placed from 3D by src/scripts/cenote.ts */
  #cenote-labels {
    position: fixed;
    inset: 0;
    z-index: 1;
    pointer-events: none;
    overflow: hidden;
    opacity: 0;
    transition: opacity 1.2s ease;
  }
  :global(.cenote-live) #cenote-labels {
    opacity: 1;
  }
  #cenote-labels :global(.cl) {
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    top: 0;
    opacity: 0;
    font: 650 12.5px/1.15 var(--font);
    letter-spacing: 0.01em;
    color: var(--foam);
    text-shadow: 0 1px 3px rgba(4, 20, 20, 0.8), 0 0 10px rgba(4, 20, 20, 0.5);
    white-space: nowrap;
    will-change: transform, opacity;
  }
  #cenote-labels :global(.cl small) {
    display: block;
    font-weight: 450;
    font-size: 11px;
    color: var(--foam-2);
  }
  #cenote-labels :global(.cl small) {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 4px;
    margin-top: 1px;
  }
  /* phones: each name is centred under its light (src/scripts/cenote.ts places it) */
  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    #cenote-labels :global(.cl) {
      text-align: center;
    }
    #cenote-labels :global(.cl small) {
      justify-content: center;
    }
  }
  #cenote-labels :global(.cl .rt) {
    display: inline-flex;
    filter: drop-shadow(0 1px 2px rgba(4, 20, 20, 0.7));
  }
  #cenote-labels :global(.cl .role) {
    font-weight: 450;
    color: var(--foam-2);
    margin-left: 6px;
  }
  /* the GM's name sits on a dark backing, so it reads over the spokes and rings round it */
  #cenote-labels :global(.cl.gm) {
    font-size: 14px;
    padding: 3px 8px 4px;
    border-radius: 9px;
    background: rgba(4, 24, 24, 0.62);
  }
  #cenote-labels :global(.cl.fact) {
    font-weight: 500;
    font-size: 11.5px;
    color: #f3e6c4;
  }
  #cenote-labels :global(.cl.mem) {
    font-size: 14px;
  }
  :global(.cenote-live) #backdrop {
    display: block;
  }
  :global(.cenote-live) #cenote {
    opacity: 1;
  }
  section {
    position: relative;
    z-index: 2;
    padding-inline: var(--gutter);
  }
  /* Without the scene each section carries its own water colour. */
  section,
  .layer {
    background: var(--bg, transparent);
  }
  /* With the scene, the water shows through; the floor sections stay solid (light text needs a
     known background, and the scene is near-black down there anyway). */
  :global(.cenote-live) section:not(.paths, .build) {
    background: transparent;
  }

  .hero {
    --bg: var(--limestone);
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 0.95fr) minmax(0, 1.05fr);
    grid-template-areas: 'h1 install' 'lede install' 'repo install' '. install';
    grid-template-rows: auto auto auto 1fr;
    column-gap: clamp(32px, 5vw, 80px);
    align-items: start;
    padding-top: clamp(24px, 6vh, 72px);
    padding-bottom: clamp(48px, 10vh, 120px);
  }
  .hero-copy {
    display: contents;
  }
  h1 {
    grid-area: h1;
    font-size: clamp(2.6rem, 6.4vw, 5.6rem);
    line-height: 0.96;
    letter-spacing: -0.035em;
    font-weight: 760;
    margin: 0 0 24px;
    max-width: 12ch;
    text-wrap: balance;
  }
  .lede {
    grid-area: lede;
    font-size: clamp(1.08rem, 1.5vw, 1.28rem);
    line-height: 1.5;
    color: var(--ink-2);
    max-width: 46ch;
    margin: 0 0 28px;
  }
  .repo {
    grid-area: repo;
    justify-self: start;
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 12px;
    padding: 12px 18px 12px 14px;
    border: 2px solid var(--ink);
    border-radius: 999px;
    text-decoration: none;
    font-weight: 650;
    font-size: clamp(1rem, 1.6vw, 1.2rem);
    background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.35);
  }
  .repo:hover {
    background: var(--ink);
    color: var(--foam);
  }
  .repo-host {
    font-weight: 450;
    opacity: 0.75;
  }
  .hero-install {
    grid-area: install;
    padding-top: clamp(4px, 2vw, 18px);
  }

  .honest {
    --bg: #bfdcd6;
    padding-block: 28px 64px;
  }
  .honest h2 {
    font-size: clamp(1.7rem, 3.4vw, 2.4rem);
    letter-spacing: -0.025em;
    line-height: 1.05;
    font-weight: 740;
    margin: 0 0 10px;
  }
  .honest p {
    max-width: 62ch;
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  .descent {
    position: relative;
    z-index: 2;
  }
  .layer {
    min-height: 92vh;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    padding-block: 12vh;
  }
  .layer[data-layer='seats'] {
    --bg: #2f8580;
  }
  .layer[data-layer='messages'] {
    --bg: var(--cenote);
    justify-content: flex-end;
  }
  .layer[data-layer='memory'] {
    --bg: #093a3c;
  }
  .layer[data-layer='approvals'] {
    --bg: var(--deep);
    justify-content: flex-end;
  }
  .panel {
    max-width: 34rem;
    padding: clamp(22px, 3vw, 34px);
    border-radius: 22px;
    background: rgba(10, 30, 30, 0.82);
    color: var(--foam);
    -webkit-backdrop-filter: blur(6px);
    backdrop-filter: blur(6px);
  }
  .panel h2 {
    font-size: clamp(1.7rem, 3.4vw, 2.6rem);
    line-height: 1.04;
    letter-spacing: -0.025em;
    font-weight: 720;
    margin: 0 0 14px;
  }
  .panel p {
    margin: 0 0 12px;
    color: var(--foam);
  }
  /* phones get one short line per panel; the full text stays on wider screens */
  .panel .short {
    display: none;
  }
  @media (max-width: 600px) {
    .panel .long {
      display: none;
    }
    .panel .short {
      display: block;
      margin: 0;
    }
    .panel h2 {
      font-size: 1.55rem;
      margin-bottom: 10px;
    }
    .panel {
      padding: 20px 20px 22px;
    }
  }
  .panel .aside {
    color: var(--foam-2);
    font-size: 0.97rem;
    margin: 0;
  }
  /* it names the colours in the animation, so it only shows while the animation runs */
  .legend {
    list-style: none;
    display: none;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 6px 16px;
    margin: 14px 0 0;
    padding: 0;
    font: 0.86rem var(--mono);
    color: var(--foam-2);
  }
  :global(.cenote-live) .legend {
    display: flex;
  }
  .legend li {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 7px;
  }
  .legend span {
    width: 9px;
    height: 9px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--c);
    box-shadow: 0 0 8px var(--c);
  }
  .panel a {
    color: #f0cf7e;
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .paths,
  .build {
    --bg: var(--abyss);
    color: var(--foam);
  }
  .paths {
    padding-top: 18vh;
    padding-bottom: 40px;
  }
  .paths h2,
  .build h2 {
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 4.4vw, 3.4rem);
    letter-spacing: -0.03em;
    line-height: 1;
    font-weight: 740;
    margin: 0 0 28px;
  }
  .path-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 18px;
    max-width: 1100px;
  }
  .path {
    display: block;
    text-decoration: none;
    padding: 26px 26px 22px;
    border: 1.5px solid #2c5a57;
    border-radius: 18px;
    background: rgba(11, 79, 82, 0.25);
  }
  .path:hover {
    border-color: var(--ochre);
  }
  .path:first-child {
    border-color: var(--maya);
    background: rgba(95, 184, 179, 0.12);
  }
  .path h3 {
    font-size: 1.45rem;
    letter-spacing: -0.015em;
    margin: 0 0 10px;
  }
  .path p {
    margin: 0 0 18px;
    color: var(--foam-2);
  }
  .path .short {
    display: none;
  }
  @media (max-width: 600px) {
    .path .long {
      display: none;
    }
    .path .short {
      display: block;
    }
    .path {
      padding: 20px 20px 18px;
    }
  }
  .go {
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--ochre-hi);
  }
  .more {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 30px 0 0;
    display: grid;
    gap: 10px;
  }
  .more a {
    color: var(--foam);
    text-underline-offset: 4px;
  }
  .build {
    padding-top: 64px;
    padding-bottom: 24px;
  }
  .build p {
    max-width: var(--measure);
    color: var(--foam-2);
  }
  .build code {
    color: var(--foam);
  }
  .links {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 12px 26px;
  }
  .links a {
    color: var(--foam);
    font-weight: 650;
    text-underline-offset: 4px;
  }

  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .hero {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
      grid-template-areas: 'h1' 'repo' 'install' 'lede';
      grid-template-rows: none;
    }
    h1 {
      margin-bottom: 18px;
    }
    .repo {
      margin-bottom: 26px;
    }
    .lede {
      margin: 32px 0 0;
    }
    .path-grid {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
    }
    /* narrow screens stack each layer: its scene (lens-shifted up in src/scripts/cenote.ts)
       draws centred in the top of the screen, and its card sits centred below it */
    .descent .layer,
    .descent .layer[data-layer] {
      justify-content: center;
      align-items: flex-end;
      min-height: 100vh;
      padding-top: 0;
      padding-bottom: 6vh;
    }
    /* the decision layer: its card and the approval card arrive together in the upper middle of
       the screen; room for the approval card is reserved directly above the panel */
    .descent .layer[data-layer='approvals'] {
      align-items: center;
      min-height: 90vh;
      padding-top: 26vh;
      padding-bottom: 4vh;
    }
    .panel {
      width: 100%;
      max-width: 34rem;
      margin-inline: auto;
    }
  }
</style>
